course: dictionary
lesson: 1273
title: Words for people who perform
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A busker is a person who plays music, sings, juggles or performs in the street or another public place. People walking past may drop coins into a hat or case to say thank you. Busking is the word for doing this work.
explain: The sentence «Behind every song, film, cartoon and painting are people doing a job: musicians, actors, animators, buskers, painters and designers» gives you a clue. Buskers are in the same list as musicians and painters, so they are people who make art. Ask yourself: who is paid by people passing by? That is the busker.
explain: The sentence «Live music is people playing right in front of you, from an orchestra in a grand hall to a busker in the street» shows the difference. An orchestra plays in a grand hall, but a busker plays in the street. Both are live music, in different places.
fact: A busker performs in a public place, such as a high street or a train station.
fact: Buskers may play guitars, violins or drums, or sing, juggle or perform.
fact: Some famous singers started out as buskers.
fact: In some places buskers need a permit before they can perform.
fact: Phrases: a street busker, a busking pitch, go busking.
exercise: «Behind every song, film, cartoon and painting are people doing a job: musicians, actors, animators, buskers, painters and designers.» What is a busker? | A person who drives a bus | A person who builds castles | A person who sells books in a shop | *A person who performs in the street for money from passers-by
exercise: «From an orchestra in a grand hall to a busker in the street» Where does a busker play? | In a grand hall | *In the street or another public place | On a farm | Inside a cinema
exercise: Lily sees a busker playing a violin on the pavement, with an open hat in front of him. What might people do? | Sell the violin to the busker | Ask the busker to water the plants | *Drop coins into the hat | Pay for a ticket to a film
test: Which word means a person who plays music in the street for money? | Orchestra | *Busker | Designer | Animator
test: Finn wants to go busking in town. What is he planning to do? | *Play or sing in a public place for money | Sell tickets for a show | Build a stage for a concert | Read stories in a library
exam: Some famous singers started out as buskers. What does this tell you? | Buskers only work in cinemas | *Busking can be a first step for people who later become famous | Buskers are always rich | Buskers are never talented
